# Upstream BusyTeX release: 649 MB, individual files up to 324 MB.
#
# It lives OUTSIDE www/ on purpose. www/ is the app — every shell loads that
# folder, and Tauri embeds all of it into the binary — so anything in there
# ships whether or not it is used. Keeping the upstream source beside the app
# instead of inside it is what stops a 649 MB tree from riding along.
#
# Fetch with:
#   curl -L https://github.com/TeXlyre/texlyre-busytex/releases/download/assets-v1.2.3/busytex-assets.tar.gz | tar xz -C engine_upstream
engine_upstream/
*.tar.gz

# www/engine/dist/ IS committed: it is build output (texmf parts + runtime),
# every file under the 50 MB git cap, regenerated by
#   node build_tools/build_slim_texmf.js

# Phase 0 compile logs (regenerated by test/run_phase0.js)
build_tools/phase0_logs/

node_modules/
tauri/target/
dist-electron/
*.log
.DS_Store
build_tools/node_modules/
